Security hardening of network and file input handling: HTTP pulls only follow same-host redirects, drop credentials on scheme or port changes and cap response bodies at 64 MiB; malformed FTP listings, truncated ENIP replies, non-UTF-8 SSH/Telnet output and malformed module text output no longer crash or abort a pull; terminal control, bidi and zero-width characters are stripped from log output; ``encrypt-results`` archives no longer expose file names (new archives need this PEAT version to decrypt); SEL serial ``rz``/``sz`` transfers run without a shell; HEAT Telnet artifact names are contained; credentials are redacted from debug config dumps; MySQL connections require TLS and follow the ``tls_verify``/``tls_ca_bundle`` settings and per-host ``https.verify`` option; FortiGate configs are parsed without generating Python source.
